# Memory Bank Management

## File Purposes

| File | Purpose | Update Frequency |
|------|---------|------------------|
| projectContext.md | Project overview, goals, constraints | Rarely (scope changes) |
| activeContext.md | Current session state, handoff info | Every session |
| systemPatterns.md | Architecture patterns, conventions | When patterns change |
| techContext.md | Technical decisions, stack details | When tech changes |
| feature-list.json | Feature tracking with pass/fail | When features complete |

## Feature List Rules

### Immutability Principle
feature-list.json entries are contracts. Once created:
- ONLY `passes` field may change (false → true)
- NEVER remove features
- NEVER edit descriptions or steps

### Modification Rules

**Allowed:**
```json
// Change passes from false to true
{"id": "1.1", "passes": false} → {"id": "1.1", "passes": true}
```

**Forbidden:**
```json
// Removing features
// Editing descriptions
// Changing steps
// Modifying IDs
```

### Deprecation Pattern
If a feature is no longer needed:
```json
{
  "id": "1.1",
  "description": "Original feature",
  "passes": false,
  "deprecated": true,
  "notes": "Superseded by 2.1"
}
```

### Verification Before Marking Complete
Before setting `passes: true`:
- [ ] All unit tests pass
- [ ] Integration tests pass (if applicable)
- [ ] E2E verification complete
- [ ] Pre-commit review approved

## Update Triggers

### Update activeContext.md When:
- Starting a session
- Completing a feature
- Making significant decisions
- Pausing work
- Encountering blockers

### Update feature-list.json When:
- Feature passes all verification
- Feature is deprecated
- Never for any other reason

### Update systemPatterns.md When:
- New architectural pattern established
- Existing pattern modified
- Pattern deprecated

### Update techContext.md When:
- New technology adopted
- Configuration changed
- Dependencies updated
